#1 - Project Documentation & URL Migration Config

What & Why

Two tightly related pieces of housekeeping that need to happen together:

Handoff documentation — Write a comprehensive AGENT.md at the project root so that any future developer or AI agent can pick this project up from scratch and understand exactly what has been built, what each file does, what environment variables are required, and what is planned next. This is portable — lives in the repo, not in Replit.
URL migration readiness — The FES Center website is currently hosted at fescenter.org/test/* (staging). When the real site launches, all paths drop /test/. Right now three places in the app/api hardcode this base URL. Centralise it into a single FESCENTER_BASE_URL environment variable on the api-server (default: https://fescenter.org/test) so the migration is a one-line config change with zero code edits.
Done looks like

AGENT.md exists at the repo root and covers: project purpose, tech stack, monorepo structure, all environment variables (name, description, where set, required/optional), all current screens and what each does, API routes, push notifications system, known limitations, future planned features, and migration notes
Every place that currently references fescenter.org/test in api-server routes uses the FESCENTER_BASE_URL env var instead
replit.md is updated to reflect recent architectural changes (news proxy route, AddEvent, inventory sheets, FESCENTER_BASE_URL)
A short "URL Migration Checklist" section in AGENT.md explains exactly what to change when migration happens (update FESCENTER_BASE_URL env var value — that's it)
Out of scope

Actually performing the URL migration (that happens when the website team is ready)
Changing any UI or functionality
Steps

Centralise FESCENTER_BASE_URL — In the api-server, read process.env.FESCENTER_BASE_URL ?? "https://fescenter.org/test" into a shared config/constants file. Replace all hardcoded fescenter.org/test strings in routes with that constant.
Audit all hardcoded URLs — Search api-server and fes-app source for any other hardcoded fescenter.org references and replace with the config constant or a clear comment.
Write AGENT.md — At the repository root, write a thorough markdown handoff document. Sections: Overview, Tech Stack, Monorepo Structure, Running Locally, Environment Variables table, Screen-by-Screen Guide, API Routes, Push Notifications, Branding/Theme, Planned Features, URL Migration Checklist, Known Issues & Limitations.
Update replit.md — Sync the existing replit.md to reflect all features built so far (news, events, investigators, inventory, notifications, push tokens DB, menu design) and the new env vars.
