#2 - News Feed Screen

What & Why

Replace the current "News" menu tile (which opens an external browser link) with a native in-app news feed. Posts are fetched from the existing WordPress site at fescenter.org/test/news/ using the WordPress REST API. Staff check news frequently, so it must load fast and feel native — paginated fetch with infinite scroll balances smoothness against network load.

Done looks like

Tapping "News" on the menu opens a native screen (not a browser)
Shows 10 most recent posts first, each as a card: hero image, title, short excerpt, date, category badge
Scrolling to the bottom of the list automatically fetches the next 10 posts (infinite scroll / load-more)
A loading skeleton or spinner shows while fetching; a retry button appears on network error
Tapping a news card opens the full article — either in a native in-app WebView or via Linking.openURL to the post's full URL
The news tile in menu.ts is updated from kind: "external" to kind: "internal" with route /news
URL is built from a configurable env/config constant (fescenter.org/test base today, easy to switch when site migrates)
Out of scope

Offline caching / persistent local storage of articles
Push notifications for new articles
In-app full article rendering (WebView link-out is acceptable for now)
Comments or social features
Steps

Config constant — Add a FESCENTER_BASE_URL constant (e.g. in constants/api.ts) set to "https://fescenter.org/test". All fetch calls in this task use that constant so migration to fescenter.org later is a one-line change.
API route in api-server — Add a /api/news proxy route that fetches from ${FESCENTER_BASE_URL}/wp-json/wp/v2/posts with query params per_page, page, _embed (for featured image), _fields=id,title,excerpt,date,link,_embedded. Proxy the paginated response and total-pages header back to the client. Proxying through the API server avoids CORS issues from the Expo client.
News screen — Create app/news.tsx. Use @tanstack/react-query with useInfiniteQuery keyed on page number. Render a FlatList with onEndReached triggering the next page fetch. Each card shows: featured image (from _embedded["wp:featuredmedia"][0].source_url), title, stripped excerpt (strip HTML tags and shortcodes), date formatted as "Feb 26, 2026", and category chips.
Skeleton & error states — Show 3 placeholder skeleton cards while the first page loads. On error show a "Could not load news — tap to retry" inline message. On end of list show "You're all caught up" footer.
Menu wiring — In constants/menu.ts change the news block from kind: "external" to kind: "internal" with route: "/news". Ensure _layout.tsx has a <Stack.Screen name="news"> entry.
