#3 - Events Screen with AddEvent

What & Why

Build the Events screen so it displays FES Center events in a clean native list and lets investigators RSVP or add events to their personal calendar. Management already uses AddEvent to manage events. The screen should pull from their existing AddEvent calendar and surface the RSVP / "Add to Calendar" flow natively. The existing events screen stub gets replaced with real data.

Done looks like

The Events screen shows a list of upcoming FES Center events fetched from AddEvent (title, date/time, location, short description)
Past events are hidden or visually de-emphasized; upcoming events shown soonest first
Tapping an event opens an event detail view with full description and an "Add to Calendar / RSVP" button
The RSVP / Add to Calendar button opens the AddEvent hosted page (or in-app WebView) so the investigator can register and add to their phone calendar
An empty state is shown when no upcoming events exist
Pull-to-refresh updates the event list
A configurable base URL constant is used (no hardcoded /test paths) — ready for URL migration
Out of scope

Building a custom RSVP form inside the app (AddEvent handles RSVP collection)
Creating or editing events from the app (admin-only, done on AddEvent dashboard)
Push notification scheduling for events (already exists in api-server notifications.ts — leave as-is)
Notes

The FES Center's existing Google Calendar (fescalendar@fescenter.org) is what AddEvent currently works alongside. The AddEvent REST API v2 (https://api.addevent.com/calevent/v2/events) can list events. If the team has not yet created an AddEvent API key, the screen should gracefully fall back to rendering the Google Calendar public iCal feed (already used by the push notifications scheduler).
AddEvent API key should be stored as a secret environment variable ADDEVENT_API_KEY, not hardcoded. The api-server proxy route reads the key server-side so it is never exposed to the mobile client.
If AddEvent API is not yet set up, implement with the existing iCal/Google Calendar feed as a fallback and leave a clear TODO comment for the AddEvent swap.
Steps

API proxy route — Add a /api/events route in the api-server that fetches events from AddEvent REST API v2 (GET /calevent/v2/events) using the ADDEVENT_API_KEY env var. If the key is absent, fall back to fetching and parsing the public Google Calendar iCal feed already used by the notifications scheduler. Return a normalized event list (id, title, start, end, location, description, addEventUrl).
Events screen — Replace the stub app/events/index.tsx with a real screen. Use @tanstack/react-query for data fetching with pull-to-refresh. Render events in a FlatList sorted by start date ascending, filtered to upcoming only. Each row shows: date badge (day + month), title, time range, location.
Event detail view — Create app/events/[id].tsx. Shows full event details and an "RSVP / Add to Calendar" button that opens the AddEvent event URL in the in-app browser (expo-web-browser) or Linking.openURL.
Empty & error states — Show "No upcoming events" with a calendar illustration when the list is empty. Show retry on fetch error.
Environment variable — Document ADDEVENT_API_KEY in the project's env documentation. The api-server should log a warning (not crash) if the key is missing and use the iCal fallback.
